findings.body:
The data source now only adds `.tabs`, so it is section **0**. `scrollToTab` still builds its index path with `section: 1`:

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/Views/TabDisplayView.swift" lines="171-181"}

`collectionView.isValid(indexPath:)` (BrowserKit `ReusableCell.swift:62`) checks `0..<numberOfSections ~= indexPath.section`. With one section that check is always false, so the guard returns early every time. Scrolling to the selected tab when the tray opens, and scrolling to a restored tab after undo-close, both silently stop working. Nothing crashes, so this is easy to miss.

The XCUITest IDs in this PR were updated from `_1_x` to `_0_x`, which confirms that tab cells now live in section 0.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/Views/TabDisplayView.swift" lines="172-172"}
        let indexPath = IndexPath(row: scrollState.toIndex, section: 0)

A cleaner option is to look up the section index from the data source (`dataSource.snapshot().indexOfSection(.tabs)`) instead of hardcoding a number.

The "scroll to the bottom" fallback was changed from `state.tabs.count - 1` to `state.tabs.count`. Only `isInactiveTabSection` was supposed to be dropped here:

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/State/TabsPanelState.swift" lines="139-144"}

`tabs.count` is one past the last row, so even with the section fixed, `isValid(indexPath:)` rejects it and the panel never scrolls to the bottom. This happens when switching between normal and private panels and the shown panel has no selected tab.

The existing test `testCreateTabScrollBehavior_forScrollToSelectedTab_noSelectedTab_returnsLastTab_ifTabsNotEmpty` still asserts `toIndex == tabCount - 1`, so it will fail with this change.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/State/TabsPanelState.swift" lines="143-143"}
                return ScrollState(toIndex: state.tabs.count - 1, withAnimation: shouldAnimate)

This PR removes `TabPanelMiddlewareActionType.refreshInactiveTabs`, but `firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/ClientTests/TabTray/TabTrayStateTests.swift:142-155` still has `testRefreshInactiveTabsAction`, which calls `getTabPanelMiddleWareAction(for: .refreshInactiveTabs)`. The whole ClientTests target will fail to compile, which contradicts the "unit tests pass" checklist item.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/Action/TabPanelAction.swift" lines="86-92"}

Delete that test. While you're there, `TabViewState.swift` still has `inactiveTabs` and `isInactiveTabsExpanded` fields that look like dead leftovers from the feature.

The diff deletes the Mozilla Public License header at the top of this file. Nothing in an inactive-tabs cleanup should touch it, and every source file in the repo is expected to carry the header (license-check tooling and reviewers look for it).

